{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as mopho/jv1080 layouts. Rows follow the LA signal path: tone common (structures pair partials 1&2 and 3&4; S = synth, P = PCM, R = ring mod) -> WG (synth: waveform + pulse width; PCM: wave pick) -> pitch envelope + LFO -> TVF + its envelope (synth partials only; PCM partials skip the TVF) -> TVA + its envelope -> part 1 / reverb context. All partial groups share one select var {p} (select.shared = 'partial', 'all' writes all four partials). Envelopes are 5-time / 3-level + sustain (TVF/TVA) and 4-time / L0-L2 + sustain + end (pitch), not DADSR, so they are plain knobs laid out T1 L1 T2 L2 ... in time order. The waveform seg and pulse-width knobs only matter for synth partials and the PCM pick only for PCM partials -- which is which depends on the structure, so nothing is dimmed ('only' keys off the select, not the structure). The part / reverb groups edit the timbre temp + system areas (not stored with the tone). The tone name is edited in the name field (name1-10 are the ascii params).",
